From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Renaud Deraison <renaud@secl.io>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:14:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] virtio: add a vhost-user-fs (virtio-fs) device

A virtio-fs device whose queues a vhost-user backend (virtiofsd) serves,
built on the vhost-user frontend the vhost-user-blk device uses: one
high-priority and one request queue, the tag and request-queue count in
config space, guest memory memfd-backed when any is configured. Set up
pre-boot from the config file's "fs" list. Creating a snapshot of a VM
with one fails (it would restore a guest whose mounts point at nothing).

The MMIO transport now answers the shared-memory region registers
(SHMSel/SHMLen/SHMBase) as the spec says a device without one must: the
length and base read as all ones. The virtio-fs driver probes them for
DAX, and failed the device on the zeros it read before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
